  "goodToKnow": "Die Mumie is a mummy, embalmed or naturally preserved: ägyptische Mumien, Moorleichen (bog bodies) in northern Germany. The most famous European one is Ötzi, a man over 5,000 years old, found by German hikers in the Ötztal Alps in 1991 and now shown in Bolzano. Mumifizieren means to mummify. Mum as a mother is Mama or Mutti. Plural: die Mumien."
